        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नारियल (nāriyal) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from nārikela, \"coconut palm and fruit\" (CDIAL 7075). CDIAL, after Bloch, takes the Sanskrit word from a Dravidian compound, comparing Tamil nāri, \"fibre\", and kēḷi, \"coconut palm\"."
            }
          ]
        },
